:: D02_Decision [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I can&apos;t stay inside forever.</p>

<p>The list of things I need writes itself in my head whether I want it to or not: real food, not dry cereal dust, something to hold my breasts in place so I can move without every step turning into a physics experiment, underwear that actually fits a body shaped like this instead of a body shaped like that. Women&apos;s basics. The phrase just sits there in my brain like a foreign object.</p>

<p>I need women&apos;s basics, because apparently, I am a woman now.</p>

<p>I stand at the front door, keys in one hand, phone in the other. <<= window.rbMoney($player.money)>> left in my checking account after rent and food. Not a lot. Enough, probably.</p>

<p>I take a deep breath, pull the hood up, keep my head down.</p>

<p>I open the door and step into the hallway. It smells the same as always, Mrs. Park&apos;s cooking drifting down from two floors up, the faint mildew smell from the leaky pipe in 3B. The stairs creak exactly the same. The front door sticks exactly the way it always has.</p>

<p>The world hasn&apos;t changed at all. It&apos;s exactly the same as it was on Wednesday when I walked out of this building as a five-nine man. The stairs don&apos;t know my hips are wider now. The mailboxes don&apos;t know my chest is different. The sidewalk has no idea my feet are three sizes smaller than they used to be.</p>

<p>I know all of it, obviously. I also know that everyone I pass today is going to look at me and see a woman they&apos;ve never seen before, and not a single one of them will ever know that two days ago I was somebody else entirely.</p>

<p>The sunlight hits my face and I squint against it. Here goes nothing.</p>

</div>

